1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,335
Part two compares six web examples, from a health check to a
controller and view.

2
00:00:06,050 --> 00:00:07,351
First example.

3
00:00:07,971 --> 00:00:09,294
Health endpoint.

4
00:00:09,744 --> 00:00:15,013
Explanation: Both servers map the same path to a small JSON
response.

5
00:00:15,717 --> 00:00:16,975
Second example.

6
00:00:17,595 --> 00:00:18,939
Routing and query.

7
00:00:19,389 --> 00:00:27,133
Explanation: ASP dot net binds the item ID. Goose parses the
path and checks the query explicitly.

8
00:00:27,842 --> 00:00:29,143
Third example.

9
00:00:29,763 --> 00:00:31,086
Ordered middleware.

10
00:00:31,536 --> 00:00:38,768
Explanation: The ID check runs before the endpoint. A rejected
request stops at the first stage.

11
00:00:39,508 --> 00:00:40,810
Fourth example.

12
00:00:41,430 --> 00:00:43,392
JSON body validation.

13
00:00:43,842 --> 00:00:50,328
Explanation: Both parse JSON and validate the fields before
sending a created response.

14
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:52,287
Fifth example.

15
00:00:52,907 --> 00:00:54,401
Request-scoped state.

16
00:00:54,851 --> 00:01:05,603
Explanation: ASP dot net shares a scoped service. Goose passes
one request-local struct by reference and updates it with the
imported add overload.

17
00:01:06,342 --> 00:01:07,664
Sixth example.

18
00:01:08,284 --> 00:01:10,332
MVC controller and view.

19
00:01:10,782 --> 00:01:19,316
Explanation: An MVC action chooses a Razor view. Goose calls a
view function and returns the same HTML.

20
00:01:20,050 --> 00:01:28,349
Here are the executable sizes. Static Goose includes the C
library. The smaller Goose build uses system libraries.

21
00:01:28,629 --> 00:01:37,354
MVC uses the self-contained dot net build because Native A O T
does not support ASP dot net MVC.

22
00:01:38,092 --> 00:01:46,113
These are application line counts and server measurements.
Each run used two thousand loopback HTTP requests.

23
00:01:46,393 --> 00:01:54,884
CPU time includes startup and shutdown. Peak memory counts the
server process. The readme explains the test setup.
